  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter `name: habeas` and the `# Habeas` title, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`. The requirement says the skill must open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps.\n\nThe first section under the title, `section[Habeas]/section[Workflow]`, is `## Workflow`. No other `##` section comes before it. It is a numbered checklist (`- [ ] 1.` and `- [ ] 2.`), which gives the ordered steps. The first step is a task-to-skill table and the second says to follow the chosen skill.\n\nThe `# Habeas` title is followed by two intro paragraphs before `## Workflow`. They are title-level prose, not a separate section, so I do not count them as breaking the requirement. The other bundled skills also have intro prose after their titles. A stricter reading would require the workflow to come immediately after the title. I judge that the wording \"before any other section\" does not support that reading as well.\n\nThe query's violation pattern is a skill that starts with a bare title and no workflow. That pattern does not occur here. I found no gap.",
